      "writtenOn": "2023-07-06T15:39:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense but the main reason of this CL is to have logging at the point where the SMCCC TRNG is used for the first time so that it is easy to identify faulty firmware when porting pvmfw to new platforms (as opposed to the silent resets we were generating).\n\nAlso, note that none of those earlier functions deal with untrusted data, are only called once (likely to be inlined) and are written in Rust (buffer overflows less likely) so stach protection wouldn\u0027t add much value there, IMO.\n\n(resolving, feel free to re-open if necessary)",
      "parentUuid": "b8278682_3d5fb854",
